Demographic & Descriptive Statistics: Includes pie charts and frequency breakdowns for respondent demographics such as age, gender, current occupation (full-time/part-time artists, hobbyists), education level, and years active on Facebook.   

Pilot Study Reliability Analysis: Documents instructions and outputs for IBM SPSS Scale Reliability Analysis using Cronbach’s Alpha. The analysis yielded an alpha value of .917, confirming high internal consistency and reliability of the questionnaire.   
  
Construct Validity Testing: Outlines steps for Factor Analysis via Dimension Reduction in SPSS to perform the Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin (KMO) Measure of Sampling Adequacy and Bartlett's Test of Sphericity (achieving a KMO of .754 and significance of $< .001$), verifying that the data is well-suited for structure detection.   

Main Survey Procedures (Sample Size = 97): Outlines statistical pathways for processing the main survey dataset collected via Google Forms. 
